# Thunderbolt mesh name service (ADR-0002).
#
# The mesh is unrouted and never reaches the UDM, so UniFi DNS cannot name it, and mDNS was
# measured non-deterministic here — `.local` names resolved to 169.254.x link-local addresses
# that change as interfaces come and go. This file is therefore the single source of mesh
# addresses; scripts/apply-mesh-hosts.sh writes it into /etc/hosts as a managed block on each
# host, which is config applied from deploy/, not hand-edited config on a node.
#
# Every service configuration references the `.mesh` names below. A raw 192.168.100.x address
# anywhere else in the repository is a review failure.
#
# Topology is a chain, not a triangle: core -- edge-a -- edge-b. Bridging all three into a
# triangle creates an L2 loop that collapses throughput and breaks external DNS.

192.168.100.11  coire-edge-a.fabric
192.168.100.12  coire-edge-b.fabric
